  <sector code="311" percentage="100" vocabulary="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to enhance climate resilience and promote water-smart agriculture in Upper Egypt by involving the private sector and developing market systems. It targets producers in key value chains and focuses on improving the capacities of businesses and civil society organizations (CSOs) to adopt and promote sustainable practices. By doing so, it seeks to improve market access, finance for agribusinesses, socioeconomic conditions for smallholder farmers, and market linkages with Dutch companies. Supported by the Embassy of the Netherlands, the project will address key challenges such as water scarcity, climate change impacts, and limited agricultural productivity, ultimately boosting the region&apos;s economic stability and food security.</narrative>
  </sector>
  <sector code="31194" percentage="50" vocabulary="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to equip selected agribusinesses to effectively support climate- and water-smart agriculture, empower civil society organizations to assist farmers in adopting these practices, and increase income and livelihood opportunities for producers in the selected value chains. By achieving these outcomes, the project is expected to enhance climate resilience and promote water-smart agriculture in Upper Egypt.</narrative>
  </sector>
